{title: The Church's One Foundation}
{artist: Samuel Stone & Samuel Wesley}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
The [D]church's one foun[G]dation is [D]Jesus Christ her [A]Lord:
she [D]is his new cre[G]ation by [D]water [A]and the [D]word.
From [A]heaven he came and [D]sought her to [Em]be his holy [A]bride;
with [D]his own blood he [G]bought her, and [D]for her [A]life he [D]died.

Verse 2
She [D]is from every [G]nation, Yet one [D]o'er all the [A]earth;
Her [D]charter of salvation, One [G]Lord, [D]one [A]faith, one [D]birth;
One [A]holy Name she [D]blesses, Partakes [Em]one holy [A]food,
And [D]to one hope [G]she presses, [D]With every [A]grace [D]endued.

Verse 3
The Church shall never perish! Her dear Lord to defend,
To guide, sustain, and cherish, Is with her to the end:
Though there be those who hate
her, And false sons in her pale,
Against or foe or traitor She ever shall prevail.

Verse 4
Though [D]with a scornful [G]wonder Men [D]see her sore [A]oppressed,
By [D]schisms rent [G]asunder, [D]By [A]heresies [D]distressed:
Yet [A]saints their watch are [D]keeping, Their cry goes [Em]up, 'How long?[A]'
And [D]soon the night of [G]weeping Shall [D]be the [A]morn of [D]song!

Verse 5
'Mid [D]toil and tribulation, [G]And [D]tumult of her [A]war,
She [D]waits the [G]consummation [D]Of [A]peace [D]forevermore;
Till, [A]with the vision [D]glorious, Her longing [Em]eyes are [A]blest,
And [D]the great Church [G]victorious Shall be [D]the [A]Church at [D]rest.
